! bss_7030.strap -- RECONSTRUCTION of the BSS processor, single segment.
!
! >>> A RECONSTRUCTION.  NOT IBM'S CODE.  No line of IBM's BSS processor
! >>> survives in any deck or document held (docs/bss_loader_spec.md 7.4,
! >>> its grep).  This program is written to C28-6379-0 pp.7-10, 12-13,
! >>> 18-19 and 22-23, read in the ink, and to the MCP loader's reading side, which is
! >>> IBM's (printed pp.324-327, transcribed).  Every convention below is
! >>> CITED to a page or marked CHOSEN; G-numbers are docs/bss_loader_spec.md
! >>> section 10's gaps.  Plan step R2a, docs/reading_notes/fortran_bss_plan.md.
!
! PAGES READ IN THE INK FOR THIS (C28-6379-0, PDF page = printed page,
! 130-400 dpi images, 2026-11-17):
!   p.7   "subprograms are assigned consecutive blocks starting from address
!         33.0, in the order in which they are encountered", "Library
!         subprograms are assigned higher locations ... in the order in which
!         calls to the library routines are encountered", "blank common
!         occupies the highest block of storage and named commons, the next
!         highest blocks"; card order A-G; the FORTRAN program card: the size
!         "either (a) the size computed at assembly time ... or (b) all 1's",
!         "The BSS processor computes the amount of space occupied".
!   p.8   Figs. 1-3, the three intermediate tables, every field used below;
!         "the largest blank common size declared by any subprogram"; "If two
!         or more subprograms declare the same named common, the largest size
!         declared is assigned"; card types 2-4.
!   p.9   card types 5-11; matching, "tries to fetch that subprogram from the
!         FORTRAN library on disk ... until all entries in the third
!         intermediate table are linked"; storage allocation steps 1-6; the
!         relocation table's contents (1)-(8); "leaves the relocation table in
!         storage, beginning at the base address of blank common"; "sorting
!         the relocation table entries so that library subprograms are loaded
!         in the order in which they appear on the disk, and printing".
!   p.10  Fig. 4, the relocation table (where it and the listing differ the
!         listing wins: the loader reads this table, spec C8, 5.4).
!   p.12  Fig. 7, the communication region (KSILO words 8-11); Phase 2 (a
!         duplicate named common: the larger size substituted, the duplicate
!         eliminated) and Phase 3 ("subtracting the amount of common from the
!         origin of the common previously computed, starting from the base
!         address of blank common"; "A second scan ... The origin of the
!         duplicate common is obtained from the entry of the same name").
!         Phases 2-3 are written for segmented jobs; used here for one
!         segment, CHOSEN, since pp.7-9 give no other order.
!   p.13  Phase 7 (the table's base not blank's base only when segmented).
!   p.17  Example 4, the storage map: the oracle, tests/check_bss_example4.py.
!   pp.18-19  Appendix A, the card formats.  The diagrams label COLUMNS and
!         print some widths (names "A8 - 64 BITS", the entry address "19
!         BITS", program size / blank common "18 BITS", common size "18
!         BITS"), and print the 5.0/5.1 flags of the data card (so its count
!         is 5.2-5.11).  The bit offsets within a column cited below (6.0-7.5,
!         7.6-8.11, 14.4, the instruction card's 10-bit count) are DERIVED
!         from those widths and the column boundaries; where a field's start
!         inside a column is not drawn, the offset is the loader's
!         (transcription) or strap2's, CHOSEN.
!   pp.22-23  Appendix B, the BSS messages, texts as printed.
! The loader's side, CITED FROM THE TRANSCRIPTIONS in decks/ (which the suite
! checks against IBM's printed machine-code column), NOT re-read in the ink
! for R2a; this header does not claim any of these lines was re-read:
! p.324 ll.12-29 (KSILO+9.32, the card count at .28, the library bit .63),
! p.325 l.23 (KSILO+9. the blank common origin), p.326 l.24 and p.327 ll.1-4
! (the common origins one half word apart from table + 2.32; the vector at
! table + 3.0 + n.32), p.327 ll.10-27 (the next table, the 36-bit library
! name, the disk address), p.327 l.28 (KSILO+10. the branch address), p.331
! ll.24-38 (ATBL: the column-1 codes), p.333 ll.22-26 (KSILO+8. and +9.).
!
! WHAT IS BUILT (R2a, staged): the scan of the subprogram decks (card
! classes 1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11 of pp.8-9), the three intermediate
! tables, matching and library fetch (repeated until every third-table entry
! is linked, so a library routine's own calls are fetched), allocation, the
! relocation table, KSILO words 8-11, the storage map, and messages.  RUN
! on the model: JOB REJECTED - COMMON AND PROGRAM OVERLAP (2), BSS
! TERMINATED JOB - PROGRAMMER ERROR with T.V. XX INCOMPLETE, ILLEGAL TYPE
! OF CARD, INCORRECT CARD ORDER and RELOCATION TABLES ARE TOO LARGE (3),
! and NO ENTRY POINT WITH NAME *MAIN* (10).  WRITTEN, NOT RUN: TOO MANY
! NAMED COMMONS, TOO MANY TRANSFER VECTORS (3), continuation program
! cards (C1), and the ERRC 20/21/22 halts below.
! NOT BUILT (each halts with a code in ERRC, never silently): the O card
! (ERRC 20), a data (block data) subprogram (22), the first table full
! (21); not written at all: sequence and check-sum checks (message 1), DEFINE
! and DEFI cards (8, 9), K, A and Z cards (not in the 1963 loader's ATBL),
! B IOD and REEL cards' storage (ignored, as other B cards), NODE cards and
! segmentation (R2c), messages 4-7, and the print through MCP.
!
! RUN (tests/check_bss_example4.py, 2026-11-17): on Example 4's subprograms
! built to p.17's sizes, the map equals the printed one row for row (ten
! subprogram rows, five common rows; the blank common origin by the test's
! chosen U), the relocation table and KSILO 8-11 equal the test's own
! reckoning of C3-C14, and messages 2, 3 and 10 print as C28 pp.22-23 word
! them, and so do message 3's ILLEGAL TYPE OF CARD, INCORRECT CARD ORDER
! and RELOCATION TABLES ARE TOO LARGE.  Measured injections in the test's
! header.  R2b (2026-11-17): this table and KSILO 8-11, fed to MCP's own
! resume load and loader, load the job as p.17 lays it out
! (tests/check_bss_mcp_load.py).
!
! SCAFFOLDING, NOT PART OF THE RECONSTRUCTION'S CLAIMS (R2b replaces them):
!   * the input: the subprogram cards are already on TWS (C28 p.7, BSS as
!     the chain's last link), here a core image at TWSA laid out as the
!     loader reads TWS -- 15 words a card, 34 cards an arc of 512 words
!     (p.332 ll.27-30) -- read by setting $4 to a card (NEXTC);
!   * the library: decks of contiguous 15-word cards and a directory at
!     LIBA (two words an entry name: the name's 48 bits; an XW whose value
!     is the deck and whose count is its cards), standing for the library's
!     LB type areas (p.327 ll.23-27, spec G7);
!   * the print: PRINT copies a 120-character A8 line to OUTB, standing for
!     MCP's print; CONB holds the console line.
!
! CHOSEN, each where it is used below, and gathered here:
!   C1 a FORTRAN program card that follows a program card is a
!      continuation: its entries only.  p.18 marks one ("Columns 6, 7, and
!      8 are blank on any subsequent continuation program cards"); the deck
!      tells it by position instead, CHOSEN.  Written, NOT RUN.
!   C2 an entry with a zero name field ends a card's entries.
!   C3 the first table has one entry per entry point (Fig. 1's "Entry Point
!      Name"); the subprogram's first entry carries its size and card count,
!      a further entry point of the same subprogram has size 0, printed
!      "E. P." (as the map prints SPTXT*).  Every entry carries the
!      subprogram's table pointers, disk address and library bit.
!   C4 the size is the card's, or, when the card's is all 1's, the scanned
!      extent; and never less than the scanned extent: the highest bit of a
!      relocatable instruction card (origin + count) or of a loading-base-0
!      data card (origin + count + secondary count), in words, rounded up.
!   C5 the second table has one entry per common definition, in deck order;
!      blank common's entry is the first, name zero.  Duplicates are found
!      after the scan (p.9 step 4, p.12 Phase 2): the earlier entry
!      survives, takes the larger amount, and the duplicate is marked in
!      Fig. 2 word 2 bit 24 (unused there) -- "a pointer" (p.12) is not
!      kept; the second scan finds the survivor by name, as Phase 3 says.
!   C6 named commons are given origins downward from blank common's base in
!      second-table order (p.12 Phase 3's subtraction, for one segment).
!   C7 blank common's base B = U - max(blank amount, relocation table size),
!      U the problem program's upper limit in KSILO+8.32 as found.  p.9 step
!      1 computes "the upper limit ..., the size of the relocation table,
!      and the origin of blank common" together; the table starts at B
!      (p.9) and must fit under U.  Not printed anywhere (G5).
!   C8 a third-table entry's word 1 is the calling subprogram's name (its
!      first entry point's), for message 3's YY; word 3 the matched name.
!   C9 the library is searched by every entry name (SPTXT* finds IOCS*'s
!      deck); a library routine's deck address is kept in Fig. 1 word 3 bits
!      46-63 (unused for a library entry) and orders the relocation table's
!      library entries ("in the order in which they appear on the disk").
!   C10 a library entry's relocation word 0 holds the 36-bit name the loader
!      reads (p.327 l.24, LF(BU,36,6)): the first six A8 characters with
!      their two high bits dropped (A6 = A8 without them, strap2/a8.py).  C28
!      Fig. 4's note says 48 bits; the listing wins (spec C8, G7).  SETTLED
!      in R2b, read in the ink: L p.327 l.24 LF(BU,36,6); C22-6728 p.82
!      Fig. 39 "SRDKAD SYN(BU, 36, 6) ... a 36-bit field containing a
!      type-area name"; ALB (A*)DD(BU,12,6),LB, L p.291 l.29.  Which name
!      (the first entry point) and the LB area's naming stay CHOSEN (G7).
!   C11 (G6) the disk address is the subprogram's first card's word offset on TWS
!      in the loader's geometry (p.327 ll.12-19 as run in R1), 18 bits; the
!      card count is its cards from the program card up to the next program
!      card or the FORTRAN branch card, which is counted in none.  SETTLED
!      in R2b: C28 p.7 (the branch card follows the last subprogram), p.9
!      item 9 (it ends the deck), p.10 Fig. 4 and C22-6728 p.82 ("cards in
!      subprogram").  The loader cannot tell (count+1 loads the same,
!      measured); check_bss_mcp_load.py's fetch count pins it.
!   C12 KSILO+8.0 gets 33.0's word, 41 octal (the problem program's lower
!      limit, p.7's first subprogram address); 8.32 is read, not written;
!      9.0 and 9.32 get B's word address, 10.0 and 10.32 *MAIN*'s absolute
!      entry, a half-word address (19 bits), 11.0 zero (no node table).
!      Only these fields are written; bits 24-31 of each half word stay as
!      found.  R2b checked that against the loader's LV, which takes bit 24
!      as a sign: harmless on this path (LR, then SV, before the LV), and
!      clearing them measured identical.
!   C13 (G16) the map's columns and header lines (p.17 prints the names, not
!      the spacing); octal as six digits, an entry as ".0" or ".4".
!   C14 a transfer-vector word is B,entry;NOP (p.8 Fig. 3 note), the
!      entry the absolute half-word address.
!   C15 table capacities (64 entry points, 63 common definitions, 128
!      transfer vectors, 60 printed lines): the guide gives none (G5).
!
! REGISTERS: $4 the card, $5-$8 and $10-$14 table walkers, $9 the print
! position, $15 linkage (LVI,$15,$+1.0 / B,routine / B,0($15)); a routine
! that calls another saves $15 with SX and restores it with LX.
!
! ERRC (a test reads its bits 0-7): 0 the map printed, the tables and KSILO set;
! 2 message 2; 3 message 3 (one of its reasons); 10 message 10; 20-22 not
! built (above); 255 still running.
!
KSILO   SYN, (8)220451.0         ! L p.171 ll.42-43, K SILO DR(BU,64),(K QUANT)
!
        SLC, (8)200000.0
! ======== THE MAIN FLOW =================================================
BSS     LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, INIT
! The scan of the input deck, to the FORTRAN branch card (p.7, p.9 item 9).
        LV, $4, TWSA
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), SCLIB
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, SCAN
! Matching (p.9): every third-table name against the first table's entry
! points; a name not found is fetched from the library and scanned, which
! may add third-table entries, until every entry is linked.
        LVI, $7, T3
MLOOP   KV, $7, T3P
        BXL, MBODY
        B, MDONE
MBODY   L(BU,48), 1.0($7)
        ST(BU,48), SNAME
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, FIND1
        L(BU,1), FOUND
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, MLIB
        L(BU,48), SNAME
        ST(BU,48), 2.0($7)       ! Fig. 3 word 3: the entry point name (C8)
        V+I, $7, 3.0
        B, MLOOP
MLIB    LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, FINDL
        L(BU,1), FOUND
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, MFETCH
        B, ETV                   ! not in the library either: message 3
MFETCH  LV, $4, 1.0($10)         ! the library deck (SCAFFOLD)
        L(BU,18), 1.28($10)
        ST(BU,18), SCLEFT
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), SCLIB
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, SCAN
        B, MLOOP                 ! the same entry again: now found
! Message 10 (p.23): no *MAIN*.
MDONE   L(BU,48), TXMAIN
        ST(BU,48), SNAME
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, FIND1
        L(BU,1), FOUND
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, ENOMN
        SV, $8, MAINE
! Allocation (p.7, p.9 step 3): subprograms from 33.0 in the order met,
! the library's after the others, in the order fetched.  Each entry point's
! absolute address (Fig. 1 word 2 bits 0-18) is its subprogram's origin,
! as a half-word address, plus its relative entry point.
        LI(BU,18), (8)41
        ST(BU,18), ORGW
        ST(BU,18), LASTO
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), LIBSEL
AL0     LVI, $5, T1
AL1     KV, $5, T1P
        BXL, AL2
        B, AL5
AL2     L(BU,1), 2.25($5)
        K(BU,1), LIBSEL
        BZAE, AL4
        L(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, AL3                 ! a further entry point (C3)
        L(BU,18), ORGW
        ST(BU,18), LASTO
        +(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        ST(BU,18), ORGW
AL3     L(BU,18), LASTO
        ST(BU,18), TMPH
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), TMPH+.18
        L(BU,19), TMPH
        +(BU,19), 2.0($5)
        ST(BU,19), 1.0($5)
AL4     V+I, $5, 3.0
        B, AL1
AL5     L(BU,1), LIBSEL
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, AL6
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), LIBSEL
        B, AL0
AL6     L(BU,18), ORGW
        ST(BU,18), PEND
! The relocation table's order (p.9): the subprograms as met, then the
! library's by deck address (C9).  ORDT: one first-entry pointer a word.
        LVI, $11, ORDT
        LVI, $5, T1
OB1     KV, $5, T1P
        BXL, OB2
        B, OB4
OB2     L(BU,1), 2.25($5)
        KI(BU,1), 0
        BZAE, OB3
        L(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, OB3
        SV, $5, 0($11)
        V+I, $11, 1.0
OB3     V+I, $5, 3.0
        B, OB1
OB4     LI(BU,18), 0
        ST(BU,18), LASTK
OB5     LI(BU,18), (8)777777
        ST(BU,18), MINK
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
        LVI, $5, T1
OB6     KV, $5, T1P
        BXL, OB7
        B, OB9
OB7     L(BU,1), 2.25($5)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, OB8
        L(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, OB8
        L(BU,18), 2.46($5)
        K(BU,18), LASTK
        BZAH, OB8
        K(BU,18), MINK
        BZAL, OB8
        ST(BU,18), MINK
        SV, $5, MINE
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
OB8     V+I, $5, 3.0
        B, OB6
OB9     L(BU,1), FOUND
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, OB10
        LV, $5, MINE
        SV, $5, 0($11)
        V+I, $11, 1.0
        L(BU,18), MINK
        ST(BU,18), LASTK
        B, OB5
OB10    SV, $11, ORDE
! The relocation table's size (p.9 step 1): per subprogram 3 words, the
! named commons' half words from 2.32, the vector from 3.0 + n.32's word
! (p.327 ll.1-4), one word a transfer.
        LI(BU,18), 0
        ST(BU,18), TT
        LVI, $11, ORDT
TS1     KV, $11, ORDE
        BXL, TS2
        B, TS3
TS2     LV, $5, 0($11)
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, SPRNG
        L(BU,18), TT
        +(BU,18), EW
        ST(BU,18), TT
        V+I, $11, 1.0
        B, TS1
! Blank common's base (C7), and RELOCATION TABLES ARE TOO LARGE when the
! table or blank common is larger than the storage under U.
TS3     L(BU,18), T2+1.28
        K(BU,18), TT
        BAH, TS4
        L(BU,18), TT
TS4     ST(BU,18), TMPB
        L(BU,18), KSILO+8.32
        K(BU,18), TMPB
        BAL, ERTL
        -(BU,18), TMPB
        ST(BU,18), BLKB
! Duplicate named commons (p.8 item 2, p.9 step 4, p.12 Phase 2): the
! earlier entry survives with the LARGEST amount (C5).
        LVI, $5, T2+2.0
DD1     KV, $5, T2P
        BXL, DD2
        B, DD6
DD2     SV, $5, CUR5
        LVI, $8, T2+2.0
DD3     KV, $8, CUR5
        BXL, DD4
        B, DD5
DD4     L(BU,1), 1.24($8)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, DD4N
        L(BU,48), 0($8)
        K(BU,48), 0($5)
        BZAE, DD4N
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), 1.24($5)
        L(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        K(BU,18), 1.28($8)
        BZAH, DD5
        ST(BU,18), 1.28($8)      ! the largest wins
        B, DD5
DD4N    V+I, $8, 2.0
        B, DD3
DD5     V+I, $5, 2.0
        B, DD1
! Origins (p.12 Phase 3): blank at B, the named ones below it in turn.
DD6     L(BU,18), BLKB
        ST(BU,18), T2+1.0
        ST(BU,18), TOP
        LVI, $5, T2+2.0
DO1     KV, $5, T2P
        BXL, DO2
        B, DO4
DO2     L(BU,1), 1.24($5)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, DO3
        L(BU,18), TOP
        -(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        ST(BU,18), TOP
        ST(BU,18), 1.0($5)
DO3     V+I, $5, 2.0
        B, DO1
! The second scan: a duplicate takes the origin of the entry of its name.
DO4     LVI, $5, T2+2.0
DO5     KV, $5, T2P
        BXL, DO6
        B, DO9
DO6     L(BU,1), 1.24($5)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, DO8
        LVI, $8, T2+2.0
DO7     L(BU,1), 1.24($8)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, DO7N
        L(BU,48), 0($8)
        K(BU,48), 0($5)
        BZAE, DO7N
        L(BU,18), 1.0($8)
        ST(BU,18), 1.0($5)
        B, DO8
DO7N    V+I, $8, 2.0
        B, DO7
DO8     V+I, $5, 2.0
        B, DO5
! p.9 step 6: common and program overlap, message 2.
DO9     L(BU,18), TOP
        K(BU,18), PEND
        BAL, EOVL
! The communication region (Fig. 7, C12).
        LI(BU,18), (8)41
        ST(BU,18), KSILO+8.0
        L(BU,18), BLKB
        ST(BU,18), KSILO+9.0
        ST(BU,18), KSILO+9.32
        LI(BU,6), 0
        ST(BU,6), KSILO+9.18
        ST(BU,6), KSILO+9.50
        LV, $8, MAINE
        L(BU,19), 1.0($8)
        ST(BU,19), KSILO+10.0
        ST(BU,19), KSILO+10.32
        LI(BU,5), 0
        ST(BU,5), KSILO+10.19
        ST(BU,5), KSILO+10.51
        LI(BU,24), 0
        ST(BU,24), KSILO+11.0
! The relocation table at B (p.9), zeroed first.
        L(BU,18), BLKB
        ST(BU,18), WA
        LV, $12, WA
        L(BU,18), TT
        ST(BU,18), TMPB
RZ1     L(BU,18), TMPB
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, RZ2
        -I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), TMPB
        LI(BU,64), 0
        ST(BU,64), 0($12)
        V+I, $12, 1.0
        B, RZ1
RZ2     LV, $12, WA
        LVI, $11, ORDT
RT1     KV, $11, ORDE
        BXL, RT2
        B, MAP
RT2     LV, $5, 0($11)
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, SPRNG
        SV, $12, TMPA
        L(BU,18), TMPA
        +(BU,18), EW
        ST(BU,18), RNXT
! Word 0 (p.324 ll.24-28, p.327 ll.11-25): the disk address and card count,
! or the library name and bit 63.
        L(BU,1), 2.25($5)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, RT3
        L(BU,18), 2.46($5)
        ST(BU,18), 0($12)
        L(BU,16), .48($5)
        ST(BU,18), .28($12)
        B, RT4
RT3     L(BU,48), 0($5)
        SF(BU,36,6), 0($12)      ! A8 to A6 (C10)
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), .63($12)
! Word 1: the origin, the vector's length, the next table (p.326 l.47).
RT4     L(BU,19), 1.0($5)
        -(BU,19), 2.0($5)
        ST(BU,19), TMPH
        L(BU,18), TMPH
        ST(BU,18), 1.0($12)
        L(BU,18), NTV
        ST(BU,18), 1.28($12)
        V+I, $11, 1.0
        KV, $11, ORDE
        BXL, RT4N
        B, RT5
RT4N    L(BU,18), RNXT
        ST(BU,18), 1.46($12)
! Word 2: the number of named commons (p.324 l.20), then each common's
! origin a half word on from 2.32 (p.326 l.24), in the subprogram's order.
RT5     L(BU,18), NCOM
        ST(BU,19), 2.0($12)
        L(BU,18), P2S
        ST(BU,18), WB
        LV, $14, WB
        L(BU,18), P2E
        ST(BU,18), WB
        SV, $12, TMPA
        LV, $13, TMPA
        V+I, $13, 2.32
RT6     KV, $14, WB
        BXL, RT6B
        B, RT7
RT6B    L(BU,18), 1.0($14)
        ST(BU,18), 0($13)
        V+I, $13, .32
        V+I, $14, 2.0
        B, RT6
! The vector (p.9 (5); Fig. 3 note), from 3.0 + n.32's word.
RT7     SV, $12, TMPA
        L(BU,18), TMPA
        +(BU,18), TVOFF
        ST(BU,18), WB
        LV, $13, WB
        L(BU,18), P3S
        ST(BU,18), WB
        LV, $14, WB
        L(BU,18), P3E
        ST(BU,18), WB
RT8     KV, $14, WB
        BXL, RT9
        B, RT10
RT9     L(BU,48), 2.0($14)
        ST(BU,48), SNAME
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, FIND1
        L(BU,64), TVSKL
        ST(BU,64), 0($13)
        L(BU,19), 1.0($8)
        ST(BU,19), 0($13)
        L(BU,64), 0($13)
        ST(BU,64), 1.0($14)      ! Fig. 3 note: "replaced by a branch; NOP"
        V+I, $13, 1.0
        V+I, $14, 3.0
        B, RT8
RT10    L(BU,18), RNXT
        ST(BU,18), WA
        LV, $12, WA
        B, RT1
! ======== THE STORAGE MAP (p.17; columns C13) ===========================
MAP     LVI, $10, HDR1
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PLINE
        LVI, $10, HDR2
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PLINE
        LVI, $5, T1
        LVI, $13, T2
MP1     KV, $13, T2P
        BXL, MP1A
        B, MP1C
MP1A    L(BU,1), 1.24($13)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, MP1C
        V+I, $13, 2.0
        B, MP1
MP1C    KV, $5, T1P
        BXL, MP3
        KV, $13, T2P
        BXL, MP6
        B, MPX
MP3     L(BU,48), 0($5)
        ST(BU,48), LINE
        L(BU,19), 1.0($5)
        -(BU,19), 2.0($5)
        ST(BU,19), TMPH
        L(BU,18), TMPH
        ST(BU,18), OCTV
        LVI, $9, LINE+1.32
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, OCT6
        L(BU,19), 2.0($5)
        ST(BU,19), TMPH
        L(BU,18), TMPH
        ST(BU,18), OCTV
        LVI, $9, LINE+3.0
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, OCT6
        LI(BU,8), (8)73
        ST(BU,8), 0($9)
        V+, $9, K8
        L(BU,1), TMPH+.18
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, MP3H
        LI(BU,8), (8)12
        B, MP3D
MP3H    LI(BU,8), 4
MP3D    ST(BU,8), 0($9)
        L(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BZAE, MP4
        LVI, $10, TXEP
        LVI, $9, LINE+4.32
        LI(BU,8), 5
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        B, MP5
MP4     ST(BU,18), OCTV
        LVI, $9, LINE+4.32
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, OCT6
MP5     LVI, $9, LINE+6.0
        L(BU,1), 2.25($5)
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, MP5Y
        LVI, $10, TXNO
        LI(BU,8), 2
        B, MP5Z
MP5Y    LVI, $10, TXYES
        LI(BU,8), 3
MP5Z    ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        V+I, $5, 3.0
MP6     L(BU,16), TXSEP
        ST(BU,16), LINE+8.0
        KV, $13, T2P
        BXL, MP8
        B, MP9
MP8     L(BU,48), 0($13)
        K(BU,48), ZEROW
        BAE, MP8A
        ST(BU,48), LINE+9.0
MP8A    L(BU,18), 1.0($13)
        ST(BU,18), OCTV
        LVI, $9, LINE+10.32
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, OCT6
        L(BU,18), 1.28($13)
        ST(BU,18), OCTV
        LVI, $9, LINE+12.0
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, OCT6
        V+I, $13, 2.0
MP9     LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PRINT
        B, MP1
MPX     LI(BU,8), 0
        B, HALT
! ======== THE SCAN (pp.7-9) =============================================
! Cards from $4: the input to the FORTRAN branch card (SCLIB 0), or a
! library deck of SCLEFT cards (SCLIB 1).  SCST: 0 before a program card,
! 1 after program and common definition cards, 2 after the first
! relocatable instruction card (the vector's data cards follow, p.9 item
! 6), 3 in the body.
SCAN    SX, $15, SCSV
        LI(BU,8), 0
        ST(BU,8), SCST
        ST(BU,1), PREVP
        ST(BU,1), CUROPEN
SCLOOP  L(BU,1), SCLIB
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, SCL2
        L(BU,18), SCLEFT
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, SCEND
SCL2    L(BU,1), PREVP
        ST(BU,1), WASP
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), PREVP
! Column 1 (ATBL, L p.331 ll.24-38; C28 pp.18-19).
        L(BU,12), 0($4)
        KI(BU,12), (8)35
        BAE, SCPROG              ! FORTRAN program 5,6,7,9
        KI(BU,12), (8)27
        BAE, SCCOM               ! common definition 5,7,8,9
        KI(BU,12), (8)25
        BAE, SCINS               ! relocatable instruction 5,7,9
        KI(BU,12), (8)17
        BAE, SCDAT               ! relocatable data 6,7,8,9
        KI(BU,12), (8)37
        BAE, SCFB                ! FORTRAN branch 5,6,7,8,9
        KI(BU,12), (8)2010
        BAE, SCORG               ! loader adjustment (O): not built
        KI(BU,12), (8)7
        BAE, SCNEXT              ! p.9 item 7: absolute binary ignored
        KI(BU,12), (8)5
        BAE, SCNEXT
        KI(BU,12), (8)15
        BAE, SCNEXT
        KI(BU,12), (8)4100
        BAE, SCNEXT              ! C, P, D (p.9 item 7)
        KI(BU,12), (8)2004
        BAE, SCNEXT
        KI(BU,12), (8)4040
        BAE, SCNEXT
        KI(BU,12), (8)1100
        BAE, SCNEXT              ! T (p.8 item 4): the sequence counter only
        KI(BU,12), (8)1300
        BAE, SCNEXT              ! super T (p.9 item 11)
        KI(BU,12), (8)4200
        BAE, SCNEXT              ! B (p.9 item 10; IOD and REEL not built)
        B, SCILL
SCNEXT  L(BU,18), CCNT
        +I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), CCNT
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, NEXTC
        L(BU,1), SCLIB
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, SCLOOP
        L(BU,18), SCLEFT
        -I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), SCLEFT
        B, SCLOOP
SCEND   LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, CLOSE
        LX, $15, SCSV
        B, 0($15)
SCFB    LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, CLOSE
        LX, $15, SCSV
        B, 0($15)
SCORG   LI(BU,8), 20
        B, HALT
! The FORTRAN program card (p.7, p.8 item 1; format C28 p.18: size 6.0-7.5,
! blank common 7.6-8.11, entries of 84 bits from 9.0, name 64 bits, the
! entry point 19 bits at 14.4).
SCPROG  L(BU,1), WASP
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, SCPRC               ! a continuation (C1)
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, CLOSE                 ! the previous subprogram's size (p.7)
        L(BU,24), T1P
        ST(BU,24), CURSP
        LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), CUROPEN
        ST(BU,1), FIRSTE
        LI(BU,24), 0
        ST(BU,24), CCNT
        ST(BU,24), EXT
        L(BU,18), .60($4)
        ST(BU,18), CSIZE
        L(BU,18), 1.14($4)
        K(BU,18), T2+1.28
        BZAH, SCPR1
        ST(BU,18), T2+1.28       ! blank common: the largest declared (p.8)
SCPR1   SV, $4, TMPA
        L(BU,1), SCLIB
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, SCPR1L
        L(BU,24), TMPA
        -(BU,24), TWSA
        ST(BU,24), TMPA
SCPR1L  L(BU,18), TMPA
        ST(BU,18), DADR          ! C11, C9
        LI(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), SCST
        L(BU,18), T2P
        ST(BU,18), CP2
        L(BU,18), T3P
        ST(BU,18), CP3
SCPRC   L(BU,8), SCST
        KI(BU,8), 1
        BZAE, SCORD
        SV, $4, TMPA
        LV, $6, TMPA
        LI(BU,8), 9
        ST(BU,8), SLOTN
SCPRL   L(BU,64), 1.32($6)
        K(BU,64), ZEROW
        BAE, SCPR9               ! C2
        LV, $5, T1P
        KV, $5, T1E
        BXL, SCPR2
        LI(BU,8), 21
        B, HALT
SCPR2   LI(BU,64), 0
        ST(BU,64), 0($5)
        ST(BU,64), 1.0($5)
        ST(BU,64), 2.0($5)
        L(BU,48), 1.32($6)
        ST(BU,48), 0($5)         ! Fig. 1 word 1: the entry point name
        L(BU,19), 2.32($6)
        ST(BU,19), 2.0($5)       ! word 3: the relative entry point
        L(BU,1), SCLIB
        ST(BU,1), 2.25($5)       ! word 3 bit 25: library
        L(BU,18), CP3
        ST(BU,18), 1.46($5)      ! word 2: the third table pointer
        L(BU,18), CP2
        ST(BU,18), 2.28($5)      ! word 3: the second table pointer
        L(BU,18), DADR
        ST(BU,18), 2.46($5)      ! word 3: the disk address
        V+I, $5, 3.0
        SV, $5, T1P
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), FIRSTE
        V+, $6, K84
        L(BU,8), SLOTN
        -I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), SLOTN
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BZAE, SCPRL
SCPR9   L(BU,1), FIRSTE
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, SCPRX
        LI(BU,8), 22             ! no entry point: a data subprogram
        B, HALT
SCPRX   LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), PREVP
        B, SCNEXT
! The common definition card (p.8 item 2; C28 p.19: names of 64 bits from
! 9.0, the size 18 bits at 14.4, 84 bits an entry).
SCCOM   L(BU,8), SCST
        KI(BU,8), 1
        BZAE, SCORD
        SV, $4, TMPA
        LV, $6, TMPA
        LI(BU,8), 9
        ST(BU,8), SLOTN
SCCL    L(BU,64), 1.32($6)
        K(BU,64), ZEROW
        BAE, SCNEXT
        LV, $5, T2P
        KV, $5, T2E
        BXL, SCC2
        B, ETMC
SCC2    LI(BU,64), 0
        ST(BU,64), 0($5)
        ST(BU,64), 1.0($5)
        L(BU,48), 1.32($6)
        ST(BU,48), 0($5)
        L(BU,18), 2.32($6)
        ST(BU,18), 1.28($5)
        V+I, $5, 2.0
        SV, $5, T2P
        V+, $6, K84
        L(BU,8), SLOTN
        -I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), SLOTN
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BZAE, SCCL
        B, SCNEXT
! The relocatable instruction card (p.9 item 5; C28 p.19: count 5 low 10
! bits, origin 6-7, data from 9.0).  The first one's first 64 bits are an
! index word, its count the vector's length (count bits 28-45: card 1.60;
! its meaning is G13, CHOSEN).
SCINS   L(BU,8), SCST
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BAE, SCORD
        KI(BU,8), 1
        BZAE, SCI2
        L(BU,18), 1.60($4)
        ST(BU,18), TVN
        LI(BU,18), 0
        ST(BU,18), TVK
        LI(BU,8), 2
        ST(BU,8), SCST
        B, SCI3
SCI2    LI(BU,8), 3
        ST(BU,8), SCST
SCI3    L(BU,24), .60($4)
        +(BU,10), .50($4)
        K(BU,24), EXT
        BZAH, SCNEXT
        ST(BU,24), EXT
        B, SCNEXT
! The relocatable data card (p.9 item 6; C28 p.19: count 5.2-5.11, origin
! 6-7, secondary count 8-9, loading base 10, data from 11.0).  Those right
! after the first instruction card hold the vector's A8 names.
SCDAT   L(BU,8), SCST
        KI(BU,8), 2
        BAL, SCORD
        L(BU,12), 1.44($4)
        KI(BU,12), 0
        BZAE, SCNEXT             ! a common's data: not the subprogram's
        L(BU,24), .60($4)
        +(BU,10), .50($4)
        +(BU,24), 1.20($4)
        K(BU,24), EXT
        BZAH, SCD1
        ST(BU,24), EXT
SCD1    L(BU,8), SCST
        KI(BU,8), 2
        BZAE, SCNEXT
        L(BU,10), .50($4)
        ST(BU,24), RB
        SV, $4, TMPA
        LV, $6, TMPA
SCDL    L(BU,24), RB
        KI(BU,24), 64
        BAL, SCNEXT
        -I(BU,24), 64
        ST(BU,24), RB
        L(BU,18), TVK
        K(BU,18), TVN
        BZAL, SCNEXT
        +I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), TVK
        LV, $5, T3P
        KV, $5, T3E
        BXL, SCD2
        B, ETMT
SCD2    LI(BU,64), 0
        ST(BU,64), 0($5)
        ST(BU,64), 1.0($5)
        ST(BU,64), 2.0($5)
        LV, $8, CURSP
        L(BU,48), 0($8)
        ST(BU,48), 0($5)         ! Fig. 3 word 1: the subprogram (C8)
        L(BU,48), 1.56($6)
        ST(BU,48), 1.0($5)       ! word 2: the transfer vector entry
        V+I, $5, 3.0
        SV, $5, T3P
        V+I, $6, 1.0
        B, SCDL
! A subprogram ends at the next program card or the branch card (p.7): its
! card count, and its size (C4), into its first entry.
CLOSE   L(BU,1), CUROPEN
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BZAE, CLX
        LV, $8, CURSP
        L(BU,18), CCNT
        ST(BU,16), .48($8)
        L(BU,24), EXT
        +I(BU,24), 63
        ST(BU,24), TMPW
        L(BU,18), TMPW
        ST(BU,18), CWDS
        L(BU,18), CSIZE
        KI(BU,18), (8)777777
        BAE, CL2
        K(BU,18), CWDS
        BAH, CL3
CL2     L(BU,18), CWDS
CL3     ST(BU,18), 1.28($8)
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), CUROPEN
CLX     B, 0($15)
! SCAFFOLD: the next card.  TWS: 15 words a card, 34 cards an arc of 512
! (p.332 ll.27-30); a library deck: contiguous.
NEXTC   V+I, $4, 15.0
        L(BU,1), SCLIB
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, NCX
        L(BU,8), ARCJ
        +I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), ARCJ
        KI(BU,8), 34
        BZAE, NCX
        V+I, $4, 2.0
        LI(BU,8), 0
        ST(BU,8), ARCJ
NCX     B, 0($15)
! ======== SUBROUTINES ===================================================
! FIND1: SNAME's 48 bits among the first table's entry points; $8, FOUND.
FIND1   LVI, $8, T1
F1LP    KV, $8, T1P
        BXL, F1B
        LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
        B, 0($15)
F1B     L(BU,48), 0($8)
        K(BU,48), SNAME
        BAE, F1HIT
        V+I, $8, 3.0
        B, F1LP
F1HIT   LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
        B, 0($15)
! FINDL (SCAFFOLD): SNAME in the library directory; $10, FOUND.
FINDL   LV, $10, LIBA
FLLP    L(BU,64), 0($10)
        K(BU,64), ZEROW
        BAE, FLNO
        L(BU,48), 0($10)
        K(BU,48), SNAME
        BAE, FLHIT
        V+I, $10, 2.0
        B, FLLP
FLNO    LI(BU,1), 0
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
        B, 0($15)
FLHIT   LI(BU,1), 1
        ST(BU,1), FOUND
        B, 0($15)
! SPRNG: for the subprogram whose first entry is $5, its second- and
! third-table ranges (to the next subprogram's pointers, or the tables'
! ends), NCOM, NTV, TVOFF = 3 + NCOM/2 (the vector's word, p.327 ll.1-4)
! and EW, its relocation entry's words.
SPRNG   L(BU,18), 1.46($5)
        ST(BU,18), P3S
        L(BU,18), 2.28($5)
        ST(BU,18), P2S
        SV, $5, TMPA
        LV, $8, TMPA
        V+I, $8, 3.0
SPR1    KV, $8, T1P
        BXL, SPR2
        L(BU,18), T2P
        ST(BU,18), P2E
        L(BU,18), T3P
        ST(BU,18), P3E
        B, SPR4
SPR2    L(BU,18), 1.28($8)
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BZAE, SPR3
        V+I, $8, 3.0
        B, SPR1
SPR3    L(BU,18), 1.46($8)
        ST(BU,18), P3E
        L(BU,18), 2.28($8)
        ST(BU,18), P2E
SPR4    L(BU,18), P2E
        -(BU,18), P2S
        ST(BU,19), TMPH
        L(BU,18), TMPH
        ST(BU,18), NCOM
        L(BU,18), P3E
        -(BU,18), P3S
        ST(BU,18), TMPB
        LI(BU,18), 0
        ST(BU,18), NTV
SPR5    L(BU,18), TMPB
        KI(BU,18), 0
        BAE, SPRX
        -I(BU,18), 3
        ST(BU,18), TMPB
        L(BU,18), NTV
        +I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), NTV
        B, SPR5
SPRX    L(BU,18), NCOM
        +I(BU,18), 6
        ST(BU,19), TMPH
        L(BU,18), TMPH
        ST(BU,18), TVOFF
        +(BU,18), NTV
        ST(BU,18), EW
        B, 0($15)
! OCT6: OCTV's 18 bits as six octal digits in A8 at $9 (A8 zero is 0o12).
OCT6    LVI, $10, 0
        LI(BU,8), 6
        ST(BU,8), OCN
OC1     L(BU,3), OCTV($10)
        KI(BU,3), 0
        BZAE, OC2
        LI(BU,8), (8)12
OC2     ST(BU,8), 0($9)
        V+, $9, K8
        V+, $10, K3
        L(BU,8), OCN
        -I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), OCN
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BZAE, OC1
        B, 0($15)
! PUTX: PXN characters from $10 to $9.
PUTX    L(BU,8), 0($10)
        ST(BU,8), 0($9)
        V+, $10, K8
        V+, $9, K8
        L(BU,8), PXN
        -I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BZAE, PUTX
        B, 0($15)
! PRINT (SCAFFOLD for MCP's print): LINE to the next 15 words of OUTB.
PRINT   LV, $9, OUTP
        LVI, $10, LINE
        LI(BU,8), 15
        ST(BU,8), PXN
PR1     L(BU,64), 0($10)
        ST(BU,64), 0($9)
        L(BU,64), BLANKW
        ST(BU,64), 0($10)
        V+I, $9, 1.0
        V+I, $10, 1.0
        L(BU,8), PXN
        -I(BU,8), 1
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        KI(BU,8), 0
        BZAE, PR1
        SV, $9, OUTP
        L(BU,18), OUTN
        +I(BU,18), 1
        ST(BU,18), OUTN
        B, 0($15)
! PLINE: the 15-word constant line at $10, printed.
PLINE   SX, $15, PLSV
        LVI, $9, LINE
        LI(BU,8), 120
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PRINT
        LX, $15, PLSV
        B, 0($15)
! INIT: the tables empty, blank common's second-table entry (C5), LINE
! blank, the print at OUTB.
INIT    SX, $15, INSV
        LVI, $5, T1
        SV, $5, T1P
        LVI, $5, T2+2.0
        SV, $5, T2P
        LVI, $5, T3
        SV, $5, T3P
        LVI, $5, OUTB
        SV, $5, OUTP
        LI(BU,64), 0
        ST(BU,64), T2
        ST(BU,64), T2+1.0
        LI(BU,8), 0
        ST(BU,8), ARCJ
        LVI, $10, BLANKL
        LVI, $9, LINE
        LI(BU,8), 120
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        LX, $15, INSV
        B, 0($15)
! ======== MESSAGES (C28 pp.22-23) =======================================
! Message 3: the console line (CONB, SCAFFOLD) and "JOB TERMINATED - "
! begun in LINE, $9 after it.
MSGBEG  SX, $15, MBSV
        LVI, $10, TXCON
        LVI, $9, CONB
        LI(BU,8), 40
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        LVI, $10, TXJT
        LVI, $9, LINE
        LI(BU,8), 17
        ST(BU,8), PXN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, PUTX
        LX, $15, MBSV
        B, 0($15)
! YY: the subprogram being scanned, or blanks.
EYY     L(BU,1), CUROPEN
        KI(BU,1), 1
        BAE, EYY1
        L(BU,48), BLANKW
        B, EYY2
EYY1    LV, $8, CURSP
        L(BU,48), 0($8)
EYY2    ST(BU,48), YYN
        B, 0($15)
ETMC    LVI, $12, TXTMC
        LI(BU,8), 26
        B, ERSN
ETMT    LVI, $12, TXTMT
        LI(BU,8), 29
        B, ERSN
SCILL   LVI, $12, TXILL
        LI(BU,8), 24
        B, ERSN
SCORD   LVI, $12, TXORD
        LI(BU,8), 24
ERSN    ST(BU,8), RSNN
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, EYY
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
        B, MSGBEG
        SV, $12, TMPA
        LV, $10, TMPA
        L(BU,8), RSNN
        ST(BU,8), PXN
